# The debug-response loop's own knobs (`tools/loop/wiggum.sh` reads this file).
#
# **The queue ends this loop, not a count.** `captures.py next` exits 3 when every capture is
# answered, and the command logs `nothing left to answer` and stops, so there is no number to guess
# here — which is why WIGGUM_MAX is 0 (never give up) and nothing else is set yet.
#
# Only the names in `wiggum.sh`'s SETTINGS_KNOBS may appear: a knob outside that list stops the
# driver rather than being silently ignored, which is the failure this file exists to avoid.
WIGGUM_MAX=0
